.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 12, 2026
.Dt DTFL_COLLECTION_ITERATE 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_collection_iterate ,
.Nm dtfl_variable_new ,
.Nm dtfl_variable_new_from ,
.Nm dtfl_variable_set ,
.Nm dtfl_variable_set_concat ,
.Nm dtfl_collection_enter_dynamic ,
.Nm dtfl_collection_leave_dynamic ,
.Nm dtfl_feedback_summary
.Nd iterate a differential dataflow fragment to a fixed point
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/iterate.h
.Ft dtfl_collection *
.Fn dtfl_collection_iterate "dtfl_collection *c" "dtfl_iterate_fn logic" "dtfl_ctx ctx"
.Ft dtfl_variable *
.Fn dtfl_variable_new "dtfl_scope *scope" "const dtfl_type *type" "const dtfl_diff *diff" "dtfl_collection **collection"
.Ft dtfl_variable *
.Fn dtfl_variable_new_from "dtfl_collection *source" "dtfl_collection **collection"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_variable_set "dtfl_variable *v" "dtfl_collection *result"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_variable_set_concat "dtfl_variable *v" "dtfl_collection *result" "dtfl_collection *addend"
.Ft dtfl_collection *
.Fn dtfl_collection_enter_dynamic "dtfl_collection *c" "size_t level"
.Ft dtfl_collection *
.Fn dtfl_collection_leave_dynamic "dtfl_collection *c" "size_t level"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_feedback_summary "const dtfl_time_class *tc" "size_t level" "uint64_t step" "uint64_t *out"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn dtfl_collection_iterate
applies the fragment
.Fa logic
to
.Fa c
repeatedly until the collection it produces stops changing, a fixed point,
or until the iteration coordinate's range is exhausted.
It builds an iterative subscope whose time is
.Fn dtfl_time_product
of the outer class and a
.Vt u64 :
one extra coordinate counts the iteration.
The source collection enters the subscope, a
.Vt dtfl_variable
is seeded from it,
.Fa logic
transforms the Variable's collection into the next iterate, the Variable is
set to that result, and the result leaves the subscope.
The
.Fa logic
callback receives the subscope and the Variable's collection and returns the
next iterate; it must build the next iterate from the Variable's collection
with the collection methods, and
.Fn dtfl_collection_iterate
consumes the returned collection.
.Fa c
must have an Abelian difference class, since iterate negates the source so
that only the delta circulates.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_collection_iterate
does not insert a consolidate for you.
A fragment that can produce cancelling differences must consolidate, or end
in
.Fn dtfl_collection_reduce ,
.Fn dtfl_collection_count
or
.Fn dtfl_collection_distinct ,
which consolidate; otherwise logically empty differences can circulate
forever and the loop will not terminate.
.Pp
A
.Vt dtfl_variable
is a recursively defined collection, the mechanism iterate is built on.
.Fn dtfl_variable_new
creates an initially empty Variable in
.Fa scope ,
an iterative subscope, and stores its collection through
.Fa collection ;
its difference class need only be a Semigroup.
.Fn dtfl_variable_new_from
creates a Variable seeded from
.Fa source
and stores the collection
.Fa source
concatenated with the feedback;
.Fa source
must have an Abelian class, as it is negated and concatenated when the
Variable is set, binding
.Li x = logic(x + source) \- source ,
a fixed point with
.Li x + source = logic(x + source) .
.Fn dtfl_variable_set
binds the Variable to
.Fa result ,
advancing every difference's iteration coordinate by one and concatenating
any negated source, then closing the loop; it consumes the Variable and
.Fa result .
.Fn dtfl_variable_set_concat
is a convenience that concatenates
.Fa addend
into
.Fa result
first; it consumes the Variable,
.Fa result
and
.Fa addend .
Variables express mutual recursion that
.Fn dtfl_collection_iterate
alone cannot, such as two collections that evolve together in one subscope.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_collection_enter_dynamic ,
.Fn dtfl_collection_leave_dynamic
and
.Fn dtfl_feedback_summary
support dynamically scoped iteration, where the inner time is a PointStamp
whose number of coordinates is a run-time
.Fa level
rather than a compile-time type
.Pq Xr dtfl_time_class 3 , the POINTSTAMP shape .
.Fn dtfl_collection_enter_dynamic
is the identity: the stream is already in the scope.
.Fn dtfl_collection_leave_dynamic
strips all but the first
.Fa level \- 1
PointStamp coordinates of every difference's time and of its capability,
which lets a difference leave one dynamic iteration level.
.Fn dtfl_feedback_summary
builds the PointStamp path summary a dynamic feedback uses at coordinate
.Fa level :
no coordinates retained
.Pq retain None ,
identity actions below the coordinate, and
.Fa step
at it, written into
.Fa out ,
which is
.Fn dtfl_summary_depth
words of
.Fa tc .
.Fa tc
must be a PointStamp class or a Product whose inner class is a PointStamp,
and
.Fa level
must be between one and the PointStamp's maximum length.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn dtfl_collection_iterate ,
.Fn dtfl_collection_enter_dynamic
and
.Fn dtfl_collection_leave_dynamic
return a new
.Vt dtfl_collection
handle the caller frees with
.Fn dtfl_collection_free .
.Fn dtfl_variable_new
and
.Fn dtfl_variable_new_from
return a
.Vt dtfl_variable
that
.Fn dtfl_variable_set
or
.Fn dtfl_variable_set_concat
consumes.
Allocation failure is reported through the panic hook, as elsewhere in the
library; a non-Abelian class where one is required, or a dynamic level out
of range, also calls the panic hook.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_collection_join 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_collection_new 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_collection_reduce 3
.Sh STANDARDS
These functions port differential dataflow's
.Fn iterate
operator and the
.Vt Variable
type from
.Pa src/operators/iterate.rs ,
and
.Fn enter_dynamic ,
.Fn leave_dynamic
and
.Fn feedback_summary
from
.Pa src/dynamic/mod.rs ,
in the pinned upstream
.Pq differential-dataflow-v0.25.1 .
